\section*{Questions in Geometric Group Theory — Q 1.1}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a mathematical result relevant to this question in the selected manuscript. A finitely generated one-relator group without any nontrivial-parameter Baumslag--Solitar subgroup is claimed hyperbolic.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} Given finite \(X\) and \(r\in F(X)\), form \(G=\langle X\mid r\rangle\). Define
\[
 \operatorname{BS}(m,n)=\langle a,t\mid ta^mt^{-1}=a^n\rangle
 \qquad(m,n\in\mathbb Z\setminus\{0\}).
\]
The source implication is
\[
 \bigl(\forall m,n\ne0,\ \operatorname{BS}(m,n)\not\hookrightarrow G\bigr)
 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad G\text{ word-hyperbolic}.
\]
It is restricted to finitely generated one-relator groups.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Intersection and commensurator bounds reduce the problem to a restricted HNN setting. Annular diagrams generate a stationary current with finite carriers; failure of expansion would give periodic line trajectories and a forbidden Baumslag--Solitar configuration, completing the hyperbolicity argument.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The main theorem settles the one-relator subcase of the first implication, with no extra power/torsion restriction. The record includes arbitrary finite-classifying-space groups and a separate subgroup question. This entry records partial support; complete coverage of the question is not established by this catalogue.

